! lrwake-bunches-output with the beam started off axis (no kicker) and an RCOL that removes particles of each bunch, so the rows reach LRWAKE out of
! bunch order and the bunches have different sizes; each particle's bunch comes from its own column, as on the
! CPU. Only an output file, so the particles must be elegant's.
C: CHARGE, TOTAL=1e-9
K: KICKER, HKICK=2e-4, VKICK=-1e-4
D: DRIF, L=1
Q1: QUAD, L=0.2, K1=0.5
Q2: QUAD, L=0.2, K1=-0.5
LR: LRWAKE, INPUTFILE="../data/lrwake.sdds", TCOLUMN="time", WXCOLUMN="WxDipole", WYCOLUMN="WyDipole", &
    WZCOLUMN="Wz", QXCOLUMN="WxQuadrupole", QYCOLUMN="WyQuadrupole", TURNS_TO_KEEP=3, RAMP_PASSES=3, &
    FACTOR=0.8, XFACTOR=1.2, YFACTOR=0.9, ZFACTOR=1.1, QXFACTOR=0.7, QYFACTOR=1.3
MAKE: LINE=(D)
CUT: RCOL, X_MAX=1.9e-4, Y_MAX=1.3e-4
BL: LINE=(C, D, CUT, Q1, D, LR, D, Q2, D)
